Find the largest 12-digit number \( N \) that satisfies the following two conditions:

- The decimal representation of \( N \) contains six digits "4" and six digits "7";
- In the decimal representation of \( N \), no four consecutive digits form the number "7444".

Calculate the lengths of the arcs of the curves given by the parametric equations.

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \left\{\begin{array}{l}
x=\left(t^{2}-2\right) \sin t+2 t \cos t \\
y=\left(2-t^{2}\right) \cos t+2 t \sin t
\end{array}\right. \\
& 0 \leq t \leq 2 \pi
\end{aligned}
$$

Given that the function $f(x)=\sin (π-ωx)\cos ωx+\cos ^{2}ωx\ (ω > 0)$ has a minimum positive period of $π$.
(I) Find the value of $ω$;
(II) The horizontal coordinates of each point on the graph of the function $y=f(x)$ are shortened to half of the original, and the vertical coordinates remain unchanged, resulting in the graph of the function $y=g(x)$. Find the minimum value of the function $y=g(x)$ on the interval $[0, \frac{π}{16}]$.

Rectangle $ABCD$ is 8 cm by 4 cm. $M$ is the midpoint of $\overline{BC}$ , and $N$ is the midpoint of $\overline{CD}$. What is the number of square centimeters in the area of region $AMCN$?

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(32,0)--(32,16)--(0,16)--cycle);
draw((0,16)--(16,0)--(32,8)--cycle);
label("$A$",(0,16),N);
label("$B$",(32,16),N);
label("$C$",(32,0),S);
label("$D$",(0,0),S);
label("$N$",(16,0),S);
label("$M$",(32,8),E);
[/asy]

In the Cartesian coordinate system, O is the origin. It is known that $\overrightarrow {p}=(-1, 2)$, A(8, 0), B(n, t), and C(ksinθ, t), where $0 \leq \theta \leq \frac{\pi}{2}$  
(1) If $\overrightarrow {AB} \perp \overrightarrow {p}$ and $|\overrightarrow {AB}|= \sqrt {5}|\overrightarrow {OA}|$, find the vector $\overrightarrow {OB}$;  
(2) If vector $\overrightarrow {AC} \parallel \overrightarrow {p}$, when k is a constant greater than 4, tsinθ reaches its maximum value of 4, find the tangent of the angle between $\overrightarrow {OA}$ and $\overrightarrow {OC}$ at this time.

Points $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ are located on $\overline{AB}$ such that $AB = 3AD = 6BC$. If a point is selected at random on $\overline{AB}$, what is the probability that it is between $C$ and $D$? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]

draw((0,0)--(12,.0000000001));
dot((0,0)); dot((4,0)); dot((10,0)); dot((12,0));
label("$A$", (0,0), S);
label("$D$", (4,0), S);
label("$C$", (10,0), S);
label("$B$", (12,0), S);

[/asy]

In the sequence $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$, $a_{1}$ and $a_{2}$ are given non-zero integers, and $a_{n+2}=\left|a_{n+1}-a_{n}\right|$:
(1) Let $a_{1}=2, a_{2}=-1$, find $a_{2008}$;
(2) Prove that it is always possible to choose infinitely many terms from $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ to form two different constant subsequences.

Among the following statements:
① After adding or subtracting the same constant from each data point in a dataset, the variance remains unchanged;
② Given a regression equation $\hat y = 3-5x$, when the variable $x$ increases by one unit, $y$ increases by an average of 5 units;
③ A linear regression equation $\hat y = \overline{b}x + \overline{a}$ must pass through the point ($\overline{x}$, $\overline{y}$);
④ There is a correlation between the points on a curve and their coordinates;
⑤ In a 2×2 contingency table, if it is calculated that $x^2 = 13.079$, then there is a 90% probability that the two variables are related.
The number of incorrect statements is ______.
